---

Recommendation: **do not adopt DINOv3 now, and do not drop SigLIP.**

What settled it: DINOv3 ViT-L/16 is usable here offline from the HF cache, but the dense local-feature test still reproduces the real failure shape. On the persisted mesh-matching subset:

| ep | truth | DINOv3 dense best | score |
|---|---|---|---:|
| ep022 | `orollingpin01` | `orollingpin01` | 0.995 |
| ep039 | `oclock01` | `oclock01` | 0.490 |
| ep025 | `obottle01` | `obottle01` | 0.742 |
| ep044 | no library object | `obottle01` | 0.484 |
| ep046 | no library object | `obottle01` | 0.538 |
| ep031 | no library object / partial | `obottle01` | 0.615 |

The decisive problem: a true clock match scored **0.490**, while no-library negatives scored **0.538** and **0.615**. So dense DINOv3 still has correct/wrong score overlap; no safe threshold falls out of this.

DINOv3 facts: `facebook/dinov3-vitl16-pretrain-lvd1689m` loads locally with `local_files_only=True`, CUDA works, model config is ViT-L/16, hidden size 1024, 24 layers, 4 register tokens. Licence is the DINOv3 License, not a permissive open-source licence. Sources: [facebookresearch/dinov3](https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov3), [DINOv3 license](https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov3/blob/main/LICENSE.md), [HF model](https://huggingface.co/facebook/dinov3-vitl16-pretrain-lvd1689m).

What I did not count: the DINOv3 re-ID proxy run. I regenerated Hands23 detections for ep030/037/048/053, but the exact pre-dedup SAM2 crop path could not be reconstructed in the host env because SAM2 dependencies were missing. Hands23 bbox crops compared identical object boxes for both hands and gave meaningless `1.0` similarities, so I rejected that as evidence.

